rtical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.622ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 717 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> be the period of revolution of the imaginary planet in years, and let <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.023ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.183ex\" height=\"1.593ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 523 704\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> be its average distance from the Sun in kilometers. We can use the following equation to solve for <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.023ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.183ex\" height=\"1.593ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 523 704\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>:\n<br><br>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.457ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.559ex\" height=\"4.044ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1143.8 3783.3 1787.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"